# Harvested third-party registries. These files hold the names of real missing
# people, copied from someone else's site under someone else's privacy notice.
# Committing them would make that copy permanent and unerasable in every clone —
# the exact opposite of what Ley 1581/2012 requires of us. The harvester and the
# importer are in the repo; the personal data stays on the machine that pulled it.
# ...but the README that explains how a harvested set must be read is not data,
# and a clone that has the harvester without the rules is worse than no clone.
# Excluding the directory itself would stop git from ever descending into it,
# so the wildcard has to exclude the *contents* and then re-admit the READMEs.
data/external/*
!data/external/*/
data/external/*/*
!data/external/*/README.md
